 "text": "Hello! How are you today? Lots of short breaks of movement help. Stand up, stretch, do some squats, then get back to typing. It's little bit of effort that keeps the ache at bay. Try using a chair with a wide cushion in the middle, or a foam pad under a standard one. A firm chair is better than a soft one. Straight is good, but not so stiff your back gets cold. A slight lean forward helps too. That's a sign you' pushing yourself too hard. Take shorter breaks, but keep moving.",
